          },
          {
            "id": 2817,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Overview",
            "value": "<p>Overall, Korea recorded the highest retirement age for both genders, while France and Italy had the lowest figures. In addition, across all six nations, men retired later than women.</p>",
            "question_id": 36627,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 2818,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<p>Regarding countries with higher retirement ages, Korean men retired at 68 years and 8 months, the highest figure among all nations, followed by Japanese men at 67 years and 4 months. Meanwhile, men in the United States and Australia stopped working at 65 years 6 months and 64 years 1 month, respectively. As for women, they showed a similar pattern, with Korean females retiring at 67 years and 2 months, slightly ahead of their Japanese counterparts at 66 years and 9 months. The figures for American and Australian women were lower, at 64 years 2 months and 63 years 5 months, in that order.</p>",
