            "value": "<p>With regard to countries with lower retirement ages, Italian men left the workforce at 58 years and 2 months, marginally higher than French men at 57 years and 4 months. Similarly, women in Italy retired at 57 years and 3 months, compared to 56 years and 9 months for their French counterparts, marking the lowest retirement age among all countries examined.</p>",
